---
title: "Harness facts"
order: "02"
summary: >-
  The harness's own facts that ParleyInn records and names: the harness, harness sessions and transcripts, hooks, turns and compaction.
---
# Harness facts

The harness's own facts, which ParleyInn records and names but never manages; of
them, ParleyInn changes only harness configuration, under I7.

- **Harness**: The external program that runs agents, such as Claude Code or the
  Agent SDK. It keeps their transcripts, compacts their context and reports to
  ParleyInn through hooks. ParleyInn records it, changes its configuration only under I7
  and never manages its transcripts or compaction⟦f:launcher⟧; of ParleyInn's components, only
  the launcher starts and controls runs in it⟦/f⟧.
- **Harness session**: The harness's own unit, which yields one transcript, plus
  one per subagent where the harness writes them apart (ASM-03). Named only when
  describing the harness, never as a ParleyInn unit.
- **Transcript**: The harness's file of what a harness session did. A
  **transcript source** is a transcript ParleyInn ingests (Ingest marker, `parinn
  ingest`); a shrunk transcript or a rewritten prefix starts a new **transcript
  generation** (REC-07). The **transcript roots** (`transcript.roots`) are the
  directories ingest reads transcripts from by default (REC-01, SEC-18). As a
  ParleyInn term, "source" is a transcript source or a trusted source; the harness's
  `source` field and §6.1's threat sources keep their own sense, as does a
  document's single source.
- **Hook**: The harness's callback into ParleyInn, carrying its **hook input**, a
  JSON object (§9.1). The core's hook handlers answer it. Events count as
  recorded by the hook handlers only for hook input the harness itself
  delivered; a hook call from inside a run's tool process is refused and
  counted (I6).⟦f:work-rooms⟧⟦f:git-tracking⟧ Git's hooks are always
  qualified, as the commit hook.⟦/f⟧⟦/f⟧
- **Turn**: One exchange between the harness and the model, from an input to the
  model reply that ends it. A **user turn** is the turn that text typed at the
  harness's own input starts (its prompt⟦f:launcher⟧, or the terminal the launcher hosts⟦/f⟧): a
  person's message in `interactive` deployment mode, a pipeline's in
  `automation`. Only the prompt a user turn's hook input reports becomes a
  `user` event; a user-role transcript line no hook input confirms is
  `harness_text`, and a delegated task is recorded with the delegating run's
  `assistant` provenance, never `user` (Delegated task).⟦f:launcher⟧ A line the launcher carried in is no user turn: the launcher
  records the carried text's commitment as its **turn trigger** (what started a
  turn, LANE-14), and ingest records the matching line as untrusted
  `harness_text` (LANE-14).⟦/f⟧ In interactive deployment mode its `user` event,
  never the model reply, is a trusted source on the node whose hook handlers
  recorded it (I2, PRV-02).
- **Compaction**: The harness replacing earlier context in the working view with
  a compaction summary when the context window fills or when asked. ParleyInn neither performs
  nor controls it (NG1); it records it and restores pins after it (I3).
  **Compaction guidance** is the text a `PreCompact` hook handler returns to
  the harness for its compaction, built only from fixed text ParleyInn ships and
  the structural fields a closed path carries (Structural field), never pin or
  record text (PIN-07, I2).
